{"caption":"The video showcases a large flat Lego mosaic of Edvard Munch's The Scream laid on a light wooden floor, bordered by red studs, with a white cabinet edge at right, a black chair leg at upper left, and a Taikamuna watermark at lower left. The camera stays fixed, while the flexible mosaic surface itself is already deforming, with pronounced creases and lifted folds moving steadily across the visible assembled plates.

A wave-like ripple passes through the left orange-red area, lifting a sharp fold, while undulations travel through the blue and yellow sky bands above the figure and the red border remains stationary in the frame. As the plates tilt, the right white-green band shifts in height, and stud highlights change across the central dark figure and surrounding color bands throughout the visible deformation of the flexible surface during the motion.

The central face becomes resolved from a blurred yellow oval into two eyes and an open mouth as the surface flexes. No hand or tool appears within the frame, and the motion remains underway.","length_note":""}
